# oracle: boundary s s s after read_data (the box is shrink-wrapped from the data box, pad 1e-4 of the data-file length, set once by read_data); 200 LJ steps with moving atoms so the faces are re-fitted at reneighboring; thermo vol, faces and press
# oracle-inputs: w117cf_shrink_sss.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-12
units lj
atom_style atomic
boundary s s s
read_data w117cf_shrink_sss.data
pair_style lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff * * 0.1 1.0
mass * 1.0
velocity all create 0.5 4711 dist gaussian
fix 1 all nve
thermo_style custom step vol xlo xhi zlo zhi press
thermo_modify format float %.17g norm no
thermo 20
run 200
